{0 owl-rllib}

Reinforcement learning on top of {{:https://github.com/owlbarn/owl}Owl}.

The package has three libraries:

- [owl-rllib] ({!Owl_rllib}): MDPs, tabular methods and dynamic programming;
  classic control environments; DQN, REINFORCE, A2C and PPO.
- [owl-rllib.llm] ({!Owl_rllib_llm}): RL for language models on a toy model
  (REINFORCE, RLOO, token-level PPO, GRPO and its variants).
- [owl-rllib.bridges] ({!Owl_rllib_bridges}): Gymnasium and VizDoom
  environments, run in a Python child process.

{1 Where to start}

- Environments: {!Owl_rllib.Ndenv} (array observations), {!Owl_rllib.Env}
  (tabular), {!Owl_rllib.Vec_env}; {!Owl_rllib.Cartpole} and the other
  classic control tasks.
- Algorithms: {!Owl_rllib.Dp}, {!Owl_rllib.Tabular}, {!Owl_rllib.Dqn},
  {!Owl_rllib.Reinforce}, {!Owl_rllib.A2c}, {!Owl_rllib.Ppo}.
- Networks and policies: {!Owl_rllib.Neural}, {!Owl_rllib.Policy}.
- Reproducibility: {!Owl_rllib.Rng}.

Most modules are functors over Owl's single ([S]) or double ([D]) precision,
with [S] and [D] instances provided. The programs in [examples/] show each
part in use.
